    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maedi</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēdi</span></b> ), ōrum,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαῖδοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thracian people on
				the borders of Macedonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 1, 1,
				§ 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4,
				11, 18, § 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 26,
				25, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">28,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Eutr. 5, 7</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mae-dĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mēd-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαιδικός</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			Mædi.—Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maedĭca</span></b> , ae, f.
			(sc. terra or regio), <i>the Mædian
			territory</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 26, 25, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">40, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22</span></i>.</div>
